{
  "version": 1,
  "claim": "Freeing every low-anchor z and fixing the Hangprinter gauge at top x=y=0, A.x=0, home at origin makes autocal anchor error (in that frame) independent of uneven low-anchor heights on HP3/HP4/HP5/HP5r (offline h=-20..+20 mm: HP3 0.97-1.02, HP4 0.69-0.70, HP5 1.00-1.06, HP5r 1.56-1.63 mm; live HP3 uneven 0.89-1.42 mm vs 7.5-13.4 before), with small cost on equal-height machines, and removes the equal-z code paths without regressions (707 tests pass).",
  "scope": "Simulation only; offline refits on existing datasets plus 21 live headless runs (mostly HP3, some HP5). No physics change.",
  "limitations": [
    "HP3 equal-height base got worse live 1.17 -> 1.35 mm (single run)",
    "HP5 jackknife rose 1.62 -> 3.28 mm while true error fell; may affect stopping",
    "Few live seeds; HP4/HP5r live untested with uneven heights",
    "D.z/stiffness coupling unchanged"
  ],
  "candidate_revision": "a7a8d179d38c4409594f5b9fbbf5d3291144fdb8",
  "candidate_tree": "b72a5c4b32d6a13afa57bb65454fbefd4dd3aaca",
